[
    {
        "content": "<p>What would be the recommended setup for formalizations that need <code>native_decide</code> but aim to provide a proof of correctness for the computation? Would the <code>native_decide</code> run in a file separate from the formalized body, in order not to taint it?</p>",
        "id": 612725508,
        "sender_full_name": "Ralf Stephan",
        "timestamp": 1784975648
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In order to prove the correctness of the <code>native_decide</code> computation, you would need to formally verify Lean's compiler, which has not been done. There is no easy way around that; even if you isolate the <code>native_decide</code> inside a sandbox, if there is a miscompilation, the result might still be wrong.</p>\n<p>In some cases, you can use <code>cbv</code>. It's a tactic that tries to symbolically evaluate terms \"by value\", i.e. mimicking the way a native evaluation of the term would do it, but it constructs a proof term for the result.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fib</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fib</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i'</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fib</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">120</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">14028366653498915298923761</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cbv</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fib</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">120</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">14028366653498915298923761</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decide</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fib</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">120</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">14028366653498915298923761</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cbv</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fib</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">120</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">14028366653498915298923761</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decide</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- failed to synthesize `Decidable`</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Given that it needs to construct proof terms and represent all the data structures (such as hash maps) as terms, it is not as efficient as native decide, but you do not need to trust its implementation, in contrast with <code>native_decide</code>.</p>",
        "id": 612726574,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Reichert",
        "timestamp": 1784976865
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks. <code>cbv</code> would use ~43 GB RAM and &gt;15min to run here, so it's out. I'll keep it in mind, though.</p>",
        "id": 612728300,
        "sender_full_name": "Ralf Stephan",
        "timestamp": 1784978820
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Can you describe the kind of computation you have to do?</p>",
        "id": 612741215,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1784991277
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>A graph of 66M nodes (max. 38bit integer) has to be built from scratch, a certificate consisting of &gt;800 cycles specifies 370k nodes of this graph. On each of those a graph-related computation is done. Lists are involved in the naive implementation but using other data structures does not seem to buy much.</p>",
        "id": 612753950,
        "sender_full_name": "Ralf Stephan",
        "timestamp": 1785002955
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>After some research, I think I will use a setup where the repo contains Lean (math), C (using the restricted ISO C subset supported by CompCert), Rocq (for the C correctness proof). This seems pretty optimal exept for the two formalization languages.</p>\n<p>This begs the question: is there a project to replace  Rocq with Lean in that setup?</p>",
        "id": 612828536,
        "sender_full_name": "Ralf Stephan",
        "timestamp": 1785079815
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've been building a project to connect compcert to lean. See <a href=\"https://github.com/gersh/leancompcert\">https://github.com/gersh/leancompcert</a></p>",
        "id": 613481100,
        "sender_full_name": "Gershon Bialer",
        "timestamp": 1785346858
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You say it will have no axioms. I don’t understand how that is possible</p>",
